<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><rss xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" version="2.0"><channel><title>World News, Today World News, Latest International News, World Breaking News, Trending News of World - Times of India</title><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world</link><description>World News Today: Read the latest world news headlines, Current International breaking news world wide. In depth analysis and top news headlines world wide.</description><language>en-gb</language><lastBuildDate>2026-10-27T10:16:37+05:30</lastBuildDate><atom:link type="application/rss+xml" rel="self" href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/rssfeeds/296589292.cms"/><copyright>Copyright:(C) Tue, 27 Oct 2026 10:16:37 IST Bennett Coleman &amp; Co. Ltd, http://in.indiatimes.com/policyterms/1554651.cms</copyright><docs>http://syndication.indiatimes.com/</docs><image><title>World News, Today World News, Latest International News, World Breaking News, Trending News of World - Times of India</title><url>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/507610.cms</url><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world</link></image><item><title><![CDATA[Ocean Mixing Barrier Shown: Dye experiment maps slow downward transport; layered structure limits exchange]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135222699.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In a recent experiment near Martha’s Vineyard, scientists introduced rhodamine dye into the Atlantic Ocean to study its behavior. The dye spread quickly in the surface waters but demonstrated a slower descent into deeper layers. Findings showed a marked difference in mixing rates, emphasizing the complexities of ocean stratification on substance movement. This research is vital for the advancement of nutrient and pollutant transport models.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/earth/in-2018-scientists-pumped-75-kg-of-red-dye-into-the-atlantic-off-marthas-vineyard-over-36-hours-they-found-mixing-inside-the-surface-layer-was-about-140-times-stronger-than-across-its-base/articleshow/135222699.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/earth/in-2018-scientists-pumped-75-kg-of-red-dye-into-the-atlantic-off-marthas-vineyard-over-36-hours-they-found-mixing-inside-the-surface-layer-was-about-140-times-stronger-than-across-its-base/articleshow/135222699.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-27T10:05:23+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135222740,imgsize-1657592.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Saudi Arabia offered Houthis $1 billion through Iran to stop attacks: Report]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135224015.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/middle-east/saudi-arabia-offered-houthis-1-billion-through-iran-to-stop-attacks-report/articleshow/135224015.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/middle-east/saudi-arabia-offered-houthis-1-billion-through-iran-to-stop-attacks-report/articleshow/135224015.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-27T09:49:09+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Abhishek Mishra</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135224052,imgsize-1221116.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Michigan woman buys 128-year-old abandoned church for $45,000 and turns it into her dream home]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135219451.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Whitney Anderson, 45, bought a 128-year-old abandoned church in Michigan for $45,000 and is turning it into her dream home. She has spent an estimated $194,000 on renovations since June 2024 and hopes to complete most of the work by 2028. As costs could reach $400,000, Anderson describes the project as the biggest gamble of her life.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/michigan-woman-whitney-anderson-45-buys-128-year-old-abandoned-church-for-45000-and-turns-it-into-dream-home-spends-194000-on-renovations-hopes-to-finish-by-2028-as-total-cost-could-reach-400000/articleshow/135219451.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/michigan-woman-whitney-anderson-45-buys-128-year-old-abandoned-church-for-45000-and-turns-it-into-dream-home-spends-194000-on-renovations-hopes-to-finish-by-2028-as-total-cost-could-reach-400000/articleshow/135219451.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-27T03:02:07+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135219458,imgsize-90405.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Meet Anders Fernstedt, homeless man living outside London’s £210 million mansion for 3.5 years]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135221538.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Anders Fernstedt, a homeless man, has lived outside a £210 million mansion in London’s Knightsbridge for three and a half years. While the 45-room property remains empty, he survives on donated food and clothes, uses power banks to read books on his phone and relies on charity services for essentials. Neighbours have gradually accepted his presence.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/meet-homeless-man-anders-fernstedt-who-has-lived-outside-londons-210-million-mansion-for-3-5-years-how-he-survives-without-money-sleeps-through-winters-and-why-neighbours-let-him-stay/articleshow/135221538.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/meet-homeless-man-anders-fernstedt-who-has-lived-outside-londons-210-million-mansion-for-3-5-years-how-he-survives-without-money-sleeps-through-winters-and-why-neighbours-let-him-stay/articleshow/135221538.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-27T04:26:10+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135221543,imgsize-128816.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[California court revives $1M lawsuit over 3-year delay in approving a homeowner’s second dwelling]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135219344.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In a legal battle, California resident Wei Shi has taken the City of Palos Verdes Estates to court, claiming excessive delays in the approval of his accessory dwelling unit application. Shi asserts that the city violated state law’s requirements for prompt reviews. Thanks to a favorable ruling from an appeals court, his lawsuit is back on track, seeking over $1 million in damages for these holdups.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2020-a-california-homeowner-applied-to-build-a-second-dwelling-on-his-property-but-says-the-city-delayed-approval-for-over-three-years-causing-more-than-1-million-in-losses-an-october-23-court-revived-his-lawsuit/articleshow/135219344.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2020-a-california-homeowner-applied-to-build-a-second-dwelling-on-his-property-but-says-the-city-delayed-approval-for-over-three-years-causing-more-than-1-million-in-losses-an-october-23-court-revived-his-lawsuit/articleshow/135219344.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-27T08:55:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135219371,imgsize-1702205.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Jessica Alba-backed baby photo contest raises $45 million for Baby2Baby to help US children in need]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135219185.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Jessica Alba, Paris Hilton and Jenna Dewan are backing the 2026 Baby of the Year contest, which has generated more than $45 million in grants for Baby2Baby since 2024. The fundraiser supports children across the US with essentials including diapers, formula, food and clothing. The winner will receive $25,000 and a national advertising campaign opportunity.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2024-jessica-alba-helped-promote-a-baby-photo-contest-that-became-a-major-charity-fundraiser-by-2026-the-campaign-had-generated-more-than-45-million-in-grants-for-baby2baby-to-help-children-in-need-across-the-us/articleshow/135219185.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2024-jessica-alba-helped-promote-a-baby-photo-contest-that-became-a-major-charity-fundraiser-by-2026-the-campaign-had-generated-more-than-45-million-in-grants-for-baby2baby-to-help-children-in-need-across-the-us/articleshow/135219185.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-27T01:49:21+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135219343,imgsize-111908.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[New Zealand cat control helps endangered southern dotterels rebound 52% in one year]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135219322.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[New Zealand's critically endangered southern dotterel population has risen by 52 percent following focused predator control efforts. Intensive campaigns targeting feral cats on Stewart Island have yielded immediate gains in breeding. The population grew from 105 birds in early 2025 to an estimated 160 in April 2026. Wildlife officials stress that ongoing management of feral cats is crucial for the bird's long-term survival.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/wildlife/in-2025-new-zealand-targeted-feral-cats-threatening-southern-dotterels-on-stewart-island-a-year-later-the-critically-endangered-birds-population-rose-from-105-to-about-160-its-biggest-annual-gain-in-32-years/articleshow/135219322.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/wildlife/in-2025-new-zealand-targeted-feral-cats-threatening-southern-dotterels-on-stewart-island-a-year-later-the-critically-endangered-birds-population-rose-from-105-to-about-160-its-biggest-annual-gain-in-32-years/articleshow/135219322.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-27T07:55:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135219335,imgsize-1950328.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[California farmer triples walnut revenue by selling directly to 300 customers from a list of 10k]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135219290.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A walnut farmer in California revolutionized his sales with a targeted email marketing campaign. Reaching out to prior cherry customers, he uncovered 300 interested buyers for his walnuts. This approach resulted in his gross revenue tripling against wholesale prices, proving that even a small customer base can boost income stability. Consequently, many farmers are now embracing direct sales strategies to lessen financial uncertainties.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2024-a-california-walnut-farmer-turned-a-small-email-experiment-into-a-major-change-in-his-business-just-300-of-10000-cherry-customers-opted-in-yet-direct-sales-helped-triple-his-walnut-crops-gross-revenue/articleshow/135219290.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2024-a-california-walnut-farmer-turned-a-small-email-experiment-into-a-major-change-in-his-business-just-300-of-10000-cherry-customers-opted-in-yet-direct-sales-helped-triple-his-walnut-crops-gross-revenue/articleshow/135219290.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-27T06:55:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135219307,imgsize-2222500.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Samoa island sees sea turtles return after invasive animals are removed, restoring wildlife]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135218009.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[The ecosystem of Nu'utele Island is flourishing thanks to successful conservation strategies that eliminated invasive species. This revitalization has enabled native flora to rebound, supporting local farmers in sustainable crop cultivation. The eradication of predatory species has also facilitated the revival of native birds, while sea turtles have finally returned to lay their eggs on the island’s shores after years of absence.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/wildlife/in-2025-teams-began-clearing-invasive-rats-and-feral-pigs-from-samoas-nuutele-island-by-october-2026-sea-turtles-were-nesting-after-decades-of-absence-ground-doves-were-breeding-and-native-seedlings-had-returned/articleshow/135218009.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/wildlife/in-2025-teams-began-clearing-invasive-rats-and-feral-pigs-from-samoas-nuutele-island-by-october-2026-sea-turtles-were-nesting-after-decades-of-absence-ground-doves-were-breeding-and-native-seedlings-had-returned/articleshow/135218009.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-27T01:24:28+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135219269,imgsize-1680856.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Delaware sinks 180-foot fishing vessel to create offshore reef, but fish population remain unmeasured]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135217057.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In a strategic move to enhance marine ecosystems, the retired fishing vessel F/V Calcasieu Pass has been sunk off the Delaware coast to function as an artificial reef. This initiative, aimed at supporting diverse aquatic species, involved meticulously clearing hazardous materials before the sinking. Environmental authorities will oversee the area, monitoring the growth and health of the marine habitats it spawns in the years to come.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/delaware-sank-a-retired-180-foot-fishing-vessel-in-august-2026-after-it-was-transferred-for-just-1-now-it-forms-an-artificial-reef-about-26-miles-offshore-although-no-increase-in-fish-populations-has-yet-been-measured/articleshow/135217057.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/delaware-sank-a-retired-180-foot-fishing-vessel-in-august-2026-after-it-was-transferred-for-just-1-now-it-forms-an-artificial-reef-about-26-miles-offshore-although-no-increase-in-fish-populations-has-yet-been-measured/articleshow/135217057.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-27T05:59:56+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135217310,imgsize-969195.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Afghan returnees face police raids, arbitrary detention in Pakistan's KP after emergency: Report]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135223253.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Afghan nationals deported from Pakistan have alleged arbitrary arrests, midnight raids and extortion in Khyber Pakhtunkhwa following the imposition of governor’s rule and a state of emergency by the Shehbaz Sharif government. Returnees said police were demanding bribes for release. Nearly 27,000 Afghan refugees have returned through Torkham in three months, amid resettlement efforts.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/pakistan/afghan-returnees-face-police-raids-arbitrary-detention-in-pakistans-kp-after-emergency-report/articleshow/135223253.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/pakistan/afghan-returnees-face-police-raids-arbitrary-detention-in-pakistans-kp-after-emergency-report/articleshow/135223253.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-27T08:29:28+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Abhishek Mishra</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135223284,imgsize-1099766.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Trump’s approval ratings slightly recover after record low last week: Report]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135222555.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[US President Donald Trump’s approval rating has increased to 32 per cent, showing a small recovery. In contrast, a recent poll indicates that registered voters prefer Democrats over Republicans by 47 percent to 36 percent. As the midterm elections approach, voter enthusiasm appears to be higher among Democrats compared to Republicans. Additionally, voters’ views on economic management have shifted, favoring Democrats slightly over Republicans.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/us-mid-term-elections/news/trumps-approval-ratings-slightly-recover-after-record-low-last-week-report/articleshow/135222555.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/us-mid-term-elections/news/trumps-approval-ratings-slightly-recover-after-record-low-last-week-report/articleshow/135222555.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-27T07:29:34+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Pranjal Pandey</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135222587,imgsize-97216.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Can Netanyahu survive another storm? Israel votes after Oct 7, Gaza and Iran wars]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135222527.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/middle-east/can-netanyahu-survive-another-storm-israel-votes-after-october-7-gaza-and-iran-wars/articleshow/135222527.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/middle-east/can-netanyahu-survive-another-storm-israel-votes-after-october-7-gaza-and-iran-wars/articleshow/135222527.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-27T07:28:52+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Abhishek Mishra</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135222577,imgsize-965387.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[7 civilians killed in Jordan strike on Syrian militants in retaliation to church attack]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/1352